# Local search must NOT be limited by .gitignore.
#
# .gitignore decides what syncs to the remote. That has nothing to do with what
# should be searchable on the machine where the agent works. Most search tools
# built on ripgrep honor .gitignore by default, which silently hides your
# private folder from the agent's own search -- and the agent then reports that
# nothing exists, confidently and wrongly.
#
# ripgrep reads .ignore at higher precedence than .gitignore, so the negations
# below win. Applies to Claude Code's Grep tool, rg on the command line, and
# anything else that respects .ignore.
#
# See docs/vault-hygiene.md.

!_private/
!memory/

# What should actually stay out of search results -- noise, not secrets:
.git/
.obsidian/
node_modules/
.trash/
